# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version
#   is usually managed by the user. However, for a project/app, it might be fine to include them.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case you'd like to ignore it, uncomment the following line:
# .Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipenv, see https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
# poetry.lock

